        "notes": [
          "Grand samples are AKAI Splendid recordings, mapped using the upstream SFZ convention (its C3 is MIDI 60). Grand and most Electric Ogg files were checked byte-for-byte against the linked Opus mirrors. The corrupt Electric ab6mp mirror file was replaced by an Opus conversion from the original FLAC; both checksums and exact source URLs are recorded per file.",
          "Upright samples are FreePats Kawai KW recordings by Gonzalo and Roberto. Bundled mono Ogg Opus derivatives were encoded from the original FLAC, truncating to nine seconds.",
          "Wurlitzer EP200 recordings are by Greg Sullivan, licensed CC BY 3.0 Unported. Credit and license links are also in public/samples/ATTRIBUTION.md.",
          "Effects, rotary, resonance and synthesized types are approximations. Rotary uses shared horn/bass modulation motors with separate paths. Unison adds one detuned stereo voice.",
          "Some high notes extend the highest recorded root by transposition; the physical Wurlitzer source has a narrower range than the 73-key instrument.",
          "Organ, Synth and Program remain decorative, as do the spec-excluded functions. Piano size classes, pedal noise, half-pedaling and per-type effect variations are unsupported."
        ]
      }
